Interpretation:
 - bound = the closed-form C-S lower bound on R'; actual R' is exact.
 - If bound>0 for a row, the floor is PROVED for it by the clean CV criterion,
   with NO exact-low computation -- purely CV(N_R) (R-only) and m_Q (Q-only).
 - CV(N_R)^2 < m_Q/(1-m_Q) is the sufficient condition; m_Q>=C(14-r,2)/91 (THM-576).
